                <pb facs="0982" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">384.11/23: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-06T18:00:00-04:00">August 6, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. Your 70, August 6, 9 a.m. The Department has not modified the position taken
                    in its 29, July 2, 5 p.m., that American nationals should be urged to leave
                    Ethiopia immediately and wishes the Legation to continue to give effect to the
                    Department’s instructions in that sense.</p>
                <p>In respect of those American nationals who may disregard the Department’s advice
                    in this matter and who as a result may later encounter difficulties, the
                    Department would of course expect you to render such assistance as may be
                    possible under the circumstances. In such a situation the Department would
                    approve your participation in the plan worked out by the British Minister in
                    cooperation with the Ethiopian authorities for the protection of British
                    nationals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
